	(text "Amiga USB-C PD Power Supply v1.1  -  Amiga 500 / 600 / 1200 (and other +5/+12/-12 V machines)\nNeeds a USB-C PD charger that offers 15 V at 3 A (45 W or more). U1 (CH224A) requests 15 V via R1 = 56k.\nU2/U4 run only while the PD contract holds (PG low -> Q1 off) and VBUS > ~11.5 V (R3/R4).\n+5 V: U2 TPS56637 -> U3 eFuse (5.64 V OVLO, ~6 A limit): 5 A continuous.  +12 V: U4, 12.36 V.  -12 V: U5 inverting, from +12 V.\nBudget: 45 W in, about 40 W out, e.g. 5 V 5 A + 12 V 1 A + -12 V 0.2 A.\nOriginal design. Spec targets only from Commodore PSU ratings and the SnCMuseum V2 board; no circuitry copied."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
